    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3e1f04f85d83637ad4f404f8199c53691470211155016045499e82d6b107c91c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under RH, the cutoff limit makes each sufficiently small f_ε an H-limit of finite natural-dilation sums and hence a member of the source's natural Beurling space; the separate, unconditional H-limit f_ε→−χ as ε↓0 then places χ in that natural closed span and completes the strengthened criterion.",
