    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_900fbece843e98a84fb9eaec27774fb0705c96f324025a5b4d45a83b29fa21e7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Failure of the unsmoothed natural sums in H, together with the universal slow-approximation bound at finite scale, motivates a summability or damping parameter rather than certifying any particular smoothing. Retaining the cutoff dependence then lets the proof couple ε to n and balance finite Dirichlet-sum error against the zeta-shift error, yielding the conditional H-rate (log log n)^(−1/3).",
