    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c4dd55fbbc0f4beb0edb1d6061fbd3893d576fd78ad666f2bfd168001299c779",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The natural-span criterion is operationalized as H-convergence of f_{ε,n} for every sufficiently small ε: pointwise Möbius cancellation identifies f_ε and then −χ, but only the later norm-convergence argument makes f_ε a natural-span witness and allows closure to recover χ. The resulting all-small-ε convergence condition is stated as equivalent to RH.",
