      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e0ffc587eafa38ef774cc3359ae19473592f6273dbefc50121f9ed02024ef1a2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The Fourier–Mellin isometry turns H-convergence of the regularized Beurling sums into convergence of a product containing ζ and a finite Möbius Dirichlet polynomial. Under RH, reciprocal-zeta approximation and Lindelöf growth combine with the unconditional symmetric zeta-ratio bound to dominate the cutoff limit; the same ratio bound is then reused without RH to remove the regulator.",
